@@ -0,0 +1,87 @@
+# Tunnel Environment: Ring / Crawler Training and Simulation
+
+This update integrates the existing `MeshTerrain._preset_tunnel()` into the unified training and demonstration scripts, so `--terrain tunnel` can now directly train and render the `ring` robot and the chain-style `crawler`.
+
+## Training
+
+### Crawler / Chain Robot, Narrower Tunnel
+
+```bash
+python ./training/train_metamaterial.py \
+  --robot crawler \
+  --terrain tunnel \
+  --episodes 500 \
+  --episode-steps 500 \
+  --tunnel-height 2.0 \
+  --run-name crawler_tunnel
+```
+
+### Ring Robot: the Default 13 Nodes Require a Taller Tunnel
+
+```bash
+python ./training/train_metamaterial.py \
+  --robot ring \
+  --terrain tunnel \
+  --episodes 500 \
+  --episode-steps 500 \
+  --tunnel-height 5.0 \
+  --run-name ring_tunnel
+```
+
+After training, the checkpoint is saved to:
+
+```text
+results/<run-name>/checkpoint_<episode>.pt
+```
+
+## Simulate / Render the Trained Policy
+
+Use the robot and terrain metadata embedded in the checkpoint:
+
+```bash
+python ./training/demo_metamaterial.py --checkpoint results/ring_tunnel/checkpoint_500.pt --follow-camera
+```
+
+Alternatively, use the latest checkpoint directly:
+
+```bash
+python ./training/demo_metamaterial.py --checkpoint latest --follow-camera
+```
+
+A compatible checkpoint can also be forced into a tunnel for testing:
+
+```bash
+python ./training/demo_metamaterial.py \
+  --checkpoint latest \
+  --terrain tunnel \
+  --tunnel-height 5.0 \
+  --follow-camera
+```
+
+## Tunnel Arguments
+
+Internally, `--terrain tunnel` is converted to:
+
+```python
+terrain_type = "mesh"
+terrain_settings = {
+    "type": "tunnel",
+    "start": ...,
+    "slope": ...,
+    "slope_height": ...,
+    "tunnel": ...,
+    "tunnel_height": ...,
+}
+```
+
+Adjustable arguments:
+
+| Argument | Meaning | Default |
+|---|---|---:|
+| `--tunnel-start` | Starting x coordinate of the tunnel ramp | `10` |
+| `--tunnel-slope` | Horizontal length of the entrance/exit ramp | `5` |
+| `--tunnel-slope-height` | Height change of the entrance/exit ramp | `1` |
+| `--tunnel-length` | Horizontal length of the constant-height central tunnel | `10` |
+| `--tunnel-height` | Vertical clearance inside the tunnel | `5` |
+
+A `crawler` can use a smaller `--tunnel-height`, such as `2.0`. The default `13`-node `ring` requires more clearance; start with `5.0`.
