+# Tunnel environment update
+
+This patch adds `--terrain tunnel` to the existing `training/train_metamaterial.py` and `training/demo_metamaterial.py`, enabling separate training/simulation of the chain-style `crawler` and the `ring` robot.
+
+Core mapping:
+
+```python
+--terrain tunnel
+# Equivalent environment arguments:
+terrain_type = "mesh"
+terrain_settings = {
+    "type": "tunnel",
+    "start": --tunnel-start,
+    "slope": --tunnel-slope,
+    "slope_height": --tunnel-slope-height,
+    "tunnel": --tunnel-length,
+    "tunnel_height": --tunnel-height,
+}
+```
+
+## Training Examples
+
+Chain robot/crawler + tunnel:
+
+```powershell
+python .\training\train_metamaterial.py --robot crawler --terrain tunnel --episodes 500 --episode-steps 500 --save-every 50 --tunnel-height 2.0
+```
+
+Ring robot/ring + tunnel:
+
+```powershell
+python .\training\train_metamaterial.py --robot ring --terrain tunnel --num-particles 13 --episodes 500 --episode-steps 500 --save-every 50 --tunnel-height 5.0
+```
+
+The default `--tunnel-height` is `5.0`, allowing the default 13-node ring to run initially. For a narrower tunnel task, reduce it gradually to `4.0`, `3.0`, `2.5`, or `2.0`. If the ring is too difficult to pass through, first use `--num-particles 10`.
+
+## Simulation/Demonstration Examples
+
+Load the robot and terrain embedded in the checkpoint:
+
+```powershell
+python .\training\demo_metamaterial.py --checkpoint .\results\your_ring_tunnel_result\checkpoint_500.pt --terrain checkpoint --policy-mode deterministic --follow-camera
+```
+
+Force the checkpoint into a tunnel for testing:
+
+```powershell
+python .\training\demo_metamaterial.py --checkpoint latest --terrain tunnel --tunnel-height 5.0 --follow-camera
+```
+
+Note: crawler and ring observation/action dimensions usually differ, so their checkpoints should not be mixed. Train `crawler_tunnel` and `ring_tunnel` separately.
